-- `for` in `main` (SPEC §11, §14): a loop by `unfold` over (the stream, the other capabilities,
-- the threaded variables), a state of `main`'s machine (SPEC §15). `main` is div,
-- so it returns the loop, which the runtime drives. `for.core.bc` is the elaborated program, as
-- `bcc desugar` prints it.
main : F i32 =
  n : i32 <- return i32[0];
  for b in bytes stdin {
    n : i32 <- return ((unbang host[add32]) (n, i32[1]));
    return (putb (&mut stdout, b))
  };
  return n
